claimed: intent-fixture-too-small — grow IntentFixture past the reference minimum (30 per class) before any gap in the arms table is defended as real. Taken BEFORE intent-domain-in-names deliberately: the fixture is the measuring instrument, and at n=24 a one-reply difference is not a difference — a mid-lane wording change already moved an arm by two. The domain is stated explicitly (meeting and scheduling intents), the deliberately hard cases are marked rather than avoided (Proposal/Request overlap, indirect phrasing, non-English, multi-intent, and out-of-domain messages that share the register of a Request), and the fact that the messages are author-written is recorded as the limitation it is. The live sweep drops to the decisive arms so a run stays minutes rather than an hour.
